    "case_for": "I would move optical lattice clocks ahead of the Higgs discovery in this discussion. The Higgs result is of exceptional scientific importance and fully mature, but the proposed individual credit must represent two very large collaborations and an accelerator project. Katori and Ye independently established complementary approaches to clocks whose precision is now repeatedly demonstrated and already enables tests of fundamental physics. This is a sharply defined experimental advance with a strong, defensible attribution.",
    "case_against": "The central reservation is historical scope: clock performance has advanced through many groups, and a prize for the invention should not imply that later milestones belong only to the two named pioneers. The eventual reach of the clocks' applications is also still growing.",
